          div.threat:nth-child(even){
          background: rgba(200,200,200,0.1);
          }

          h4 span{
          padding-right: 1em;
          }

        </style></head><body><h1 class="title" tabindex="0">Threat Modeling Report</h1><span tabindex="0">
          Created on 13/09/2026 10:01:23 pm</span><p tabindex="0"><strong>Threat Model Name: </strong></p><p tabindex="0"><strong>Owner: </strong></p><p tabindex="0"><strong>Reviewer: </strong></p><p tabindex="0"><strong>Contributors: </strong></p><p tabindex="0"><strong>Description: </strong></p><p tabindex="0"><strong>Assumptions: </strong></p><p tabindex="0"><strong>External Dependencies: </strong></p><br /><h3 tabindex="0">Threat Model Summary:</h3><table><tr tabindex="0" role="row"><td>Not Started</td><td>135</td></tr><tr tabindex="0" role="row"><td>Not Applicable</td><td>0</td></tr><tr tabindex="0" role="row"><td>Needs Investigation</td><td>0</td></tr><tr tabindex="0" role="row"><td>Mitigation Implemented</td><td>0</td></tr><tr tabindex="0" role="row"><td>Total</td><td>135</td></tr><tr tabindex="0" role="row"><td>Total Migrated</td><td>0</td></tr></table><p class="bugtrack" /><hr /><h2 tabindex="0">
            Diagram: Diagram 1</h2><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Diagram 1 diagram screenshot&#xA;            " /><h3 tabindex="0">Diagram 1 Diagram Summary:
          </h3><table><tr tabindex="0" role="row"><td>Not Started</td><td>135</td></tr><tr tabindex="0" role="row"><td>Not Applicable</td><td>0</td></tr><tr tabindex="0" role="row"><td>Needs Investigation</td><td>0</td></tr><tr tabindex="0" role="row"><td>Mitigation Implemented</td><td>0</td></tr><tr tabindex="0" role="row"><td>Total</td><td>135</td></tr><tr tabindex="0" role="row"><td>Total Migrated</td><td>0</td></tr></table><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Account Lookup</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Account Lookup interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t1"><span>1. Spoofing the Authenticate User Process</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Authenticate User may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to User Accounts DB. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t2"><span>2. Spoofing of Destination Data Store User Accounts DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">User Accounts DB may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being written to the attacker's target instead of User Accounts DB. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t3"><span>3. Potential SQL Injection Vulnerability for User Accounts DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Tampering</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">SQL injection is an attack in which malicious code is inserted into strings that are later passed to an instance of SQL Server for parsing and execution. Any procedure that constructs SQL statements should be reviewed for injection vulnerabilities because SQL Server will execute all syntactically valid queries that it receives. Even parameterized data can be manipulated by a skilled and determined attacker.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t4"><span>4. The User Accounts DB Data Store Could Be Corrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Tampering</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Account Lookup may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to corruption of User Accounts DB. Ensure the integrity of the data flow to the data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t5"><span>5. Data Store Denies User Accounts DB Potentially Writing Data</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">User Accounts DB claims that it did not write data received from an entity on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t6"><span>6. Data Flow Sniffing</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Information Disclosure</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Account Lookup may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t7"><span>7. Potential Excessive Resource Consumption for Authenticate User or User Accounts DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Does Authenticate User or User Accounts DB take explicit steps to control resource consumption? Resource consumption attacks can be hard to deal with, and there are times that it makes sense to let the OS do the job. Be careful that your resource requests don't deadlock, and that they do timeout.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t8"><span>8. Data Flow Account Lookup Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t9"><span>9. Data Store Inaccessible</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Account/role
information</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Account/role&#xD;&#xA;information interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t10"><span>10. Spoofing the Authenticate User Process</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Authenticate User may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by User Accounts DB. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t11"><span>11. Spoofing of Source Data Store User Accounts DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">User Accounts DB may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to incorrect data delivered to Authenticate User. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t12"><span>12. Potential Data Repudiation by Authenticate User</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Authenticate User claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t13"><span>13. Weak Access Control for a Resource</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Information Disclosure</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Improper data protection of User Accounts DB can allow an attacker to read information not intended for disclosure. Review authorization settings.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t14"><span>14. Potential Process Crash or Stop for Authenticate User</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Authenticate User crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t15"><span>15. Data Flow Account/role information Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t16"><span>16. Data Store Inaccessible</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t17"><span>17. Authenticate User May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">User Accounts DB may be able to remotely execute code for Authenticate User.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t18"><span>18. Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in Authenticate User</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An attacker may pass data into Authenticate User in order to change the flow of program execution within Authenticate User to the attacker's choosing.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Account/role
information</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Account/role&#xD;&#xA;information interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t19"><span>19. Spoofing the Authenticate User Process</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Authenticate User may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to User Accounts DB. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t20"><span>20. Spoofing of Destination Data Store User Accounts DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">User Accounts DB may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being written to the attacker's target instead of User Accounts DB. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t21"><span>21. Potential SQL Injection Vulnerability for User Accounts DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Tampering</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">SQL injection is an attack in which malicious code is inserted into strings that are later passed to an instance of SQL Server for parsing and execution. Any procedure that constructs SQL statements should be reviewed for injection vulnerabilities because SQL Server will execute all syntactically valid queries that it receives. Even parameterized data can be manipulated by a skilled and determined attacker.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t22"><span>22. The User Accounts DB Data Store Could Be Corrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Tampering</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Account/role information may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to corruption of User Accounts DB. Ensure the integrity of the data flow to the data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t23"><span>23. Data Store Denies User Accounts DB Potentially Writing Data</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">User Accounts DB claims that it did not write data received from an entity on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t24"><span>24. Data Flow Sniffing</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Information Disclosure</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Account/role information may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t25"><span>25. Potential Excessive Resource Consumption for Authenticate User or User Accounts DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Does Authenticate User or User Accounts DB take explicit steps to control resource consumption? Resource consumption attacks can be hard to deal with, and there are times that it makes sense to let the OS do the job. Be careful that your resource requests don't deadlock, and that they do timeout.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t26"><span>26. Data Flow Account/role information Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t27"><span>27. Data Store Inaccessible</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Admin credentials</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Admin credentials interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t28"><span>28. Spoofing the Admin Order Management Process</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Admin Order Management may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by Admin. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t29"><span>29. Spoofing the Admin External Entity</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Admin may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Admin Order Management. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t30"><span>30. Potential Lack of Input Validation for Admin Order Management</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Tampering</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Admin credentials may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to a denial of service attack against Admin Order Management or an elevation of privilege attack against Admin Order Management or an information disclosure by Admin Order Management. Failure to verify that input is as expected is a root cause of a very large number of exploitable issues. Consider all paths and the way they handle data. Verify that all input is verified for correctness using an approved list input validation approach.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t31"><span>31. Potential Data Repudiation by Admin Order Management</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Admin Order Management claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t32"><span>32. Data Flow Sniffing</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Information Disclosure</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Admin credentials may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t33"><span>33. Potential Process Crash or Stop for Admin Order Management</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Admin Order Management crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t34"><span>34. Data Flow Admin credentials Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t35"><span>35. Elevation Using Impersonation</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Admin Order Management may be able to impersonate the context of Admin in order to gain additional privilege.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t36"><span>36. Admin Order Management May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Admin may be able to remotely execute code for Admin Order Management.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t37"><span>37. Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in Admin Order Management</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An attacker may pass data into Admin Order Management in order to change the flow of program execution within Admin Order Management to the attacker's choosing.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t38"><span>38. Cross Site Request Forgery</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Cross-site request forgery (CSRF or XSRF) is a type of attack in which an attacker forces a user's browser to make a forged request to a vulnerable site by exploiting an existing trust relationship between the browser and the vulnerable web site.  In a simple scenario, a user is logged in to web site A using a cookie as a credential.  The other browses to web site B.  Web site B returns a page with a hidden form that posts to web site A.  Since the browser will carry the user's cookie to web site A, web site B now can take any action on web site A, for example, adding an admin to an account.  The attack can be used to exploit any requests that the browser automatically authenticates, e.g. by session cookie, integrated authentication, IP whitelisting. The attack can be carried out in many ways such as by luring the victim to a site under control of the attacker, getting the user to click a link in a phishing email, or hacking a reputable web site that the victim will visit. The issue can only be resolved on the server side by requiring that all authenticated state-changing requests include an additional piece of secret payload (canary or CSRF token) which is known only to the legitimate web site and the browser and which is protected in transit through SSL/TLS. See the Forgery Protection property on the flow stencil for a list of mitigations.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Charge request/
Refund request</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Charge request/&#xD;&#xA;Refund request interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t39"><span>39. Spoofing of the Payment Gateway External Destination Entity</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Payment Gateway may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being sent to the attacker's target instead of Payment Gateway. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t40"><span>40. External Entity Payment Gateway Potentially Denies Receiving Data</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Payment Gateway claims that it did not receive data from a process on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t41"><span>41. Data Flow Charge request/ Refund request Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Credentials</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Credentials interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t42"><span>42. Spoofing the Authenticate User Process</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Authenticate User may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by Customer. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t43"><span>43. Spoofing the Customer External Entity</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Customer may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Authenticate User. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t44"><span>44. Potential Lack of Input Validation for Authenticate User</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Tampering</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Credentials may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to a denial of service attack against Authenticate User or an elevation of privilege attack against Authenticate User or an information disclosure by Authenticate User. Failure to verify that input is as expected is a root cause of a very large number of exploitable issues. Consider all paths and the way they handle data. Verify that all input is verified for correctness using an approved list input validation approach.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t45"><span>45. Potential Data Repudiation by Authenticate User</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Authenticate User claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t46"><span>46. Data Flow Sniffing</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Information Disclosure</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Credentials may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t47"><span>47. Potential Process Crash or Stop for Authenticate User</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Authenticate User crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t48"><span>48. Data Flow Credentials Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t49"><span>49. Elevation Using Impersonation</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Authenticate User may be able to impersonate the context of Customer in order to gain additional privilege.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t50"><span>50. Authenticate User May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Customer may be able to remotely execute code for Authenticate User.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t51"><span>51. Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in Authenticate User</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An attacker may pass data into Authenticate User in order to change the flow of program execution within Authenticate User to the attacker's choosing.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t52"><span>52. Cross Site Request Forgery</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Cross-site request forgery (CSRF or XSRF) is a type of attack in which an attacker forces a user's browser to make a forged request to a vulnerable site by exploiting an existing trust relationship between the browser and the vulnerable web site.  In a simple scenario, a user is logged in to web site A using a cookie as a credential.  The other browses to web site B.  Web site B returns a page with a hidden form that posts to web site A.  Since the browser will carry the user's cookie to web site A, web site B now can take any action on web site A, for example, adding an admin to an account.  The attack can be used to exploit any requests that the browser automatically authenticates, e.g. by session cookie, integrated authentication, IP whitelisting. The attack can be carried out in many ways such as by luring the victim to a site under control of the attacker, getting the user to click a link in a phishing email, or hacking a reputable web site that the victim will visit. The issue can only be resolved on the server side by requiring that all authenticated state-changing requests include an additional piece of secret payload (canary or CSRF token) which is known only to the legitimate web site and the browser and which is protected in transit through SSL/TLS. See the Forgery Protection property on the flow stencil for a list of mitigations.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Decrement stock</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Decrement stock interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t53"><span>53. Spoofing the Update Inventory Process</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Update Inventory may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Product/ Inventory DB. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t54"><span>54. Spoofing of Destination Data Store Product/ Inventory DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Product/ Inventory DB may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being written to the attacker's target instead of Product/ Inventory DB. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t55"><span>55. Potential SQL Injection Vulnerability for Product/ Inventory DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Tampering</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">SQL injection is an attack in which malicious code is inserted into strings that are later passed to an instance of SQL Server for parsing and execution. Any procedure that constructs SQL statements should be reviewed for injection vulnerabilities because SQL Server will execute all syntactically valid queries that it receives. Even parameterized data can be manipulated by a skilled and determined attacker.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t56"><span>56. The Product/ Inventory DB Data Store Could Be Corrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Tampering</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Decrement stock may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to corruption of Product/ Inventory DB. Ensure the integrity of the data flow to the data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t57"><span>57. Data Store Denies Product/ Inventory DB Potentially Writing Data</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Product/ Inventory DB claims that it did not write data received from an entity on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t58"><span>58. Data Flow Sniffing</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Information Disclosure</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Decrement stock may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t59"><span>59. Potential Excessive Resource Consumption for Update Inventory or Product/ Inventory DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Does Update Inventory or Product/ Inventory DB take explicit steps to control resource consumption? Resource consumption attacks can be hard to deal with, and there are times that it makes sense to let the OS do the job. Be careful that your resource requests don't deadlock, and that they do timeout.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t60"><span>60. Data Flow Decrement stock Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t61"><span>61. Data Store Inaccessible</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Email request</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Email request interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t62"><span>62. Spoofing of the Email Service Provider External Destination Entity</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Email Service Provider may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being sent to the attacker's target instead of Email Service Provider. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t63"><span>63. External Entity Email Service Provider Potentially Denies Receiving Data</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Email Service Provider claims that it did not receive data from a process on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t64"><span>64. Data Flow Email request Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Inventory update</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Inventory update interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t65"><span>65. Elevation Using Impersonation</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Update Inventory may be able to impersonate the context of Checkout Service in order to gain additional privilege.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Order confirmation data</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Order confirmation data interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t66"><span>66. Elevation Using Impersonation</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Send Order Confirmation may be able to impersonate the context of Checkout Service in order to gain additional privilege.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Order total</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Order total interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t67"><span>67. Elevation Using Impersonation</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Process Payment may be able to impersonate the context of Checkout Service in order to gain additional privilege.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Payment result/
Refund result</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Payment result/&#xD;&#xA;Refund result interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t68"><span>68. Spoofing the Process Payment Process</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Process Payment may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by Payment Gateway. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t69"><span>69. Spoofing the Payment Gateway External Entity</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Payment Gateway may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Process Payment. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t70"><span>70. Potential Lack of Input Validation for Process Payment</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Tampering</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Payment result/ Refund result may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to a denial of service attack against Process Payment or an elevation of privilege attack against Process Payment or an information disclosure by Process Payment. Failure to verify that input is as expected is a root cause of a very large number of exploitable issues. Consider all paths and the way they handle data. Verify that all input is verified for correctness using an approved list input validation approach.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t71"><span>71. Potential Data Repudiation by Process Payment</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Process Payment claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t72"><span>72. Data Flow Sniffing</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Information Disclosure</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Payment result/ Refund result may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t73"><span>73. Potential Process Crash or Stop for Process Payment</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Process Payment crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t74"><span>74. Data Flow Payment result/ Refund result Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t75"><span>75. Elevation Using Impersonation</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Process Payment may be able to impersonate the context of Payment Gateway in order to gain additional privilege.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t76"><span>76. Process Payment May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Payment Gateway may be able to remotely execute code for Process Payment.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t77"><span>77. Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in Process Payment</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An attacker may pass data into Process Payment in order to change the flow of program execution within Process Payment to the attacker's choosing.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t78"><span>78. Cross Site Request Forgery</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Cross-site request forgery (CSRF or XSRF) is a type of attack in which an attacker forces a user's browser to make a forged request to a vulnerable site by exploiting an existing trust relationship between the browser and the vulnerable web site.  In a simple scenario, a user is logged in to web site A using a cookie as a credential.  The other browses to web site B.  Web site B returns a page with a hidden form that posts to web site A.  Since the browser will carry the user's cookie to web site A, web site B now can take any action on web site A, for example, adding an admin to an account.  The attack can be used to exploit any requests that the browser automatically authenticates, e.g. by session cookie, integrated authentication, IP whitelisting. The attack can be carried out in many ways such as by luring the victim to a site under control of the attacker, getting the user to click a link in a phishing email, or hacking a reputable web site that the victim will visit. The issue can only be resolved on the server side by requiring that all authenticated state-changing requests include an additional piece of secret payload (canary or CSRF token) which is known only to the legitimate web site and the browser and which is protected in transit through SSL/TLS. See the Forgery Protection property on the flow stencil for a list of mitigations.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Payment result/
Refund result</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Payment result/&#xD;&#xA;Refund result interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t79"><span>79. Spoofing of the Payment Gateway External Destination Entity</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Payment Gateway may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being sent to the attacker's target instead of Payment Gateway. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t80"><span>80. External Entity Payment Gateway Potentially Denies Receiving Data</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Payment Gateway claims that it did not receive data from a process on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t81"><span>81. Data Flow Payment result/ Refund result Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Payment status/
Refund status</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Payment status/&#xD;&#xA;Refund status interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t82"><span>82. Spoofing of Source Data Store Orders DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Orders DB may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to incorrect data delivered to Payment Gateway. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t83"><span>83. External Entity Payment Gateway Potentially Denies Receiving Data</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Payment Gateway claims that it did not receive data from a process on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t84"><span>84. Weak Access Control for a Resource</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Information Disclosure</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Improper data protection of Orders DB can allow an attacker to read information not intended for disclosure. Review authorization settings.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t85"><span>85. Data Flow Payment status/ Refund status Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t86"><span>86. Data Store Inaccessible</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Read/write orders</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Read/write orders interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t87"><span>87. Spoofing the Admin Order Management Process</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Admin Order Management may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by Orders DB. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t88"><span>88. Spoofing of Source Data Store Orders DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Orders DB may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to incorrect data delivered to Admin Order Management. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t89"><span>89. Potential Data Repudiation by Admin Order Management</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Admin Order Management claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t90"><span>90. Weak Access Control for a Resource</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Information Disclosure</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Improper data protection of Orders DB can allow an attacker to read information not intended for disclosure. Review authorization settings.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t91"><span>91. Potential Process Crash or Stop for Admin Order Management</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Admin Order Management crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t92"><span>92. Data Flow Read/write orders Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t93"><span>93. Data Store Inaccessible</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t94"><span>94. Admin Order Management May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Orders DB may be able to remotely execute code for Admin Order Management.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t95"><span>95. Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in Admin Order Management</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An attacker may pass data into Admin Order Management in order to change the flow of program execution within Admin Order Management to the attacker's choosing.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Read/write orders</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Read/write orders interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t96"><span>96. Spoofing the Admin Order Management Process</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Admin Order Management may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Orders DB. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t97"><span>97. Spoofing of Destination Data Store Orders DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Orders DB may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being written to the attacker's target instead of Orders DB. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t98"><span>98. Potential SQL Injection Vulnerability for Orders DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Tampering</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">SQL injection is an attack in which malicious code is inserted into strings that are later passed to an instance of SQL Server for parsing and execution. Any procedure that constructs SQL statements should be reviewed for injection vulnerabilities because SQL Server will execute all syntactically valid queries that it receives. Even parameterized data can be manipulated by a skilled and determined attacker.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t99"><span>99. The Orders DB Data Store Could Be Corrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Tampering</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Read/write orders may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to corruption of Orders DB. Ensure the integrity of the data flow to the data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t100"><span>100. Data Store Denies Orders DB Potentially Writing Data</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Orders DB claims that it did not write data received from an entity on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t101"><span>101. Data Flow Sniffing</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Information Disclosure</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Read/write orders may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t102"><span>102. Potential Excessive Resource Consumption for Admin Order Management or Orders DB</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Does Admin Order Management or Orders DB take explicit steps to control resource consumption? Resource consumption attacks can be hard to deal with, and there are times that it makes sense to let the OS do the job. Be careful that your resource requests don't deadlock, and that they do timeout.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t103"><span>103. Data Flow Read/write orders Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t104"><span>104. Data Store Inaccessible</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Refund request</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Refund request interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t105"><span>105. Elevation Using Impersonation</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Process Payment may be able to impersonate the context of Admin Order Management in order to gain additional privilege.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Refund request</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Refund request interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t106"><span>106. Elevation Using Impersonation</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Admin Order Management may be able to impersonate the context of Process Payment in order to gain additional privilege.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Refund result</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Refund result interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t107"><span>107. Elevation Using Impersonation</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Process Payment may be able to impersonate the context of Admin Order Management in order to gain additional privilege.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Session validation</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Session validation interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t108"><span>108. Spoofing the Authenticate User Process</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Authenticate User may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Session Store. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t109"><span>109. Spoofing of Destination Data Store Session Store</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Session Store may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being written to the attacker's target instead of Session Store. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t110"><span>110. The Session Store Data Store Could Be Corrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Tampering</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Session validation may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to corruption of Session Store. Ensure the integrity of the data flow to the data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t111"><span>111. Data Store Denies Session Store Potentially Writing Data</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Session Store claims that it did not write data received from an entity on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t112"><span>112. Data Flow Sniffing</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Information Disclosure</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Session validation may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t113"><span>113. Potential Excessive Resource Consumption for Authenticate User or Session Store</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Does Authenticate User or Session Store take explicit steps to control resource consumption? Resource consumption attacks can be hard to deal with, and there are times that it makes sense to let the OS do the job. Be careful that your resource requests don't deadlock, and that they do timeout.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t114"><span>114. Data Flow Session validation Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t115"><span>115. Data Store Inaccessible</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Session validation</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Session validation interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t116"><span>116. Spoofing the Authenticate User Process</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Authenticate User may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by Session Store. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t117"><span>117. Spoofing of Source Data Store Session Store</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Session Store may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to incorrect data delivered to Authenticate User. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source data store.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t118"><span>118. Potential Data Repudiation by Authenticate User</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Authenticate User claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t119"><span>119. Weak Access Control for a Resource</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Information Disclosure</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Improper data protection of Session Store can allow an attacker to read information not intended for disclosure. Review authorization settings.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t120"><span>120. Potential Process Crash or Stop for Authenticate User</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Authenticate User crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t121"><span>121. Data Flow Session validation Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t122"><span>122. Data Store Inaccessible</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t123"><span>123. Authenticate User May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Session Store may be able to remotely execute code for Authenticate User.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t124"><span>124. Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in Authenticate User</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An attacker may pass data into Authenticate User in order to change the flow of program execution within Authenticate User to the attacker's choosing.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /><h3 tabindex="0">
      Interaction: Shipping address+
cart contents</h3><img tabindex="0" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Shipping address+&#xD;&#xA;cart contents interaction screenshot&#xA;      " /><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t125"><span>125. Spoofing the Checkout Service Process</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Checkout Service may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by Customer. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t126"><span>126. Spoofing the Customer External Entity</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Spoofing</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Customer may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Checkout Service. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t127"><span>127. Potential Lack of Input Validation for Checkout Service</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Tampering</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Shipping address+ cart contents may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to a denial of service attack against Checkout Service or an elevation of privilege attack against Checkout Service or an information disclosure by Checkout Service. Failure to verify that input is as expected is a root cause of a very large number of exploitable issues. Consider all paths and the way they handle data. Verify that all input is verified for correctness using an approved list input validation approach.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t128"><span>128. Potential Data Repudiation by Checkout Service</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Repudiation</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Checkout Service claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t129"><span>129. Data Flow Sniffing</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Information Disclosure</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Data flowing across Shipping address+ cart contents may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t130"><span>130. Potential Process Crash or Stop for Checkout Service</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Checkout Service crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t131"><span>131. Data Flow Shipping address+ cart contents Is Potentially Interrupted</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Denial Of Service</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t132"><span>132. Elevation Using Impersonation</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Checkout Service may be able to impersonate the context of Customer in order to gain additional privilege.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t133"><span>133. Checkout Service May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Customer may be able to remotely execute code for Checkout Service.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t134"><span>134. Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in Checkout Service</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">An attacker may pass data into Checkout Service in order to change the flow of program execution within Checkout Service to the attacker's choosing.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><div class="threat"><h4 tabindex="0" id="&#xA;          t135"><span>135. Cross Site Request Forgery</span> 
        [State: Not Started] 
        [Priority: High] 
        </h4><table role="grid"><tr><td id="threat-title-category" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Category:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-category">Elevation Of Privilege</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-description" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Description:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-description">Cross-site request forgery (CSRF or XSRF) is a type of attack in which an attacker forces a user's browser to make a forged request to a vulnerable site by exploiting an existing trust relationship between the browser and the vulnerable web site.  In a simple scenario, a user is logged in to web site A using a cookie as a credential.  The other browses to web site B.  Web site B returns a page with a hidden form that posts to web site A.  Since the browser will carry the user's cookie to web site A, web site B now can take any action on web site A, for example, adding an admin to an account.  The attack can be used to exploit any requests that the browser automatically authenticates, e.g. by session cookie, integrated authentication, IP whitelisting. The attack can be carried out in many ways such as by luring the victim to a site under control of the attacker, getting the user to click a link in a phishing email, or hacking a reputable web site that the victim will visit. The issue can only be resolved on the server side by requiring that all authenticated state-changing requests include an additional piece of secret payload (canary or CSRF token) which is known only to the legitimate web site and the browser and which is protected in transit through SSL/TLS. See the Forgery Protection property on the flow stencil for a list of mitigations.</td></tr><tr><td id="threat-title-justification" role="rowheader" tabindex="0"><strong>Justification:</strong></td><td class="infotd" tabindex="0" role="gridcell" headers="threat-title-justification">&lt;no mitigation provided&gt;</td></tr></table></div><br /></body></html>